Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 21:06:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 111/143] ASoC: sunxi: sun55i-a523-codec: cancel jack scan work
 on probe failure

The jack scan delayed work is scheduled from the card machine_init(), which
runs inside devm_snd_soc_register_card(). The teardown that cancels it is a
devres action registered only after card registration succeeds, so if the
card fails to register after machine_init() already scheduled the work, the
work stays pending and fires ~2s later against freed driver memory
(regmap/scodec): a use-after-free. Use devm_delayed_work_autocancel() so the
work is always cancelled on unwind, including that failure window.
---
 sound/soc/sunxi/sun55i-a523-codec.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun55i-a523-codec.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun55i-a523-codec.c
index 2a4ef5db6..c79530be5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun55i-a523-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun55i-a523-codec.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/devm-helpers.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/input.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
@@ -1459,7 +1460,10 @@ static int sun55i_codec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	/* Jack parameters (OPi4A: level 1, threshold 8, debounce 0) */
 	jack = &scodec->jack;
 	mutex_init(&jack->lock);
-	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&jack->scan_work, sun55i_codec_jack_scan_work);
+	ret = devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &jack->scan_work,
+					   sun55i_codec_jack_scan_work);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "jack scan work init failed\n");
 	jack->first_report = true;
 	jack->irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);
 	jack->det_level = !device_property_read_bool(dev,
